next: **CRAN SUBMISSION ON HOLD — user called a hold 2026-08-17 00:52 MDT; do NOT submit or merge dev->main without explicit go-ahead.** **HOLD UPDATE 2026-10-13: no CRAN submission of RMediation until BOTH RMediation and medfit are mature (user decision; "mature" is not yet defined, so ask before treating any date or green check as the trigger).** **Policy update 2026-10-12 (grill ledger `planning/GRILL-semfit-dependency-policy-2026-10-12.md`): the `method="gauss"` default hold is lifted (no CRAN reverse dependencies; NEWS + retained `hcubature` mitigate); submission and dev->main still need an explicit go-ahead; CRAN gets 1.7.1 from a `release/1.7.1` branch that omits the SEMFit route (held until medfit 0.8.0 is on CRAN, then Suggests >= 0.8.0).** v1.7.0 is published on GitHub as a PRE-RELEASE only (tag `v1.7.0` on `dev`); `main` deliberately remains at 1.6.1, which is what CRAN serves. Users can get the fix via `remotes::install_github("Data-Wise/RMediation", ref = "dev")`. v1.7.0 fixes issue #27: `pprodnormal3()` returned silently wrong probabilities on ill-conditioned covariance (24% error at rho=0.999, 92% relative in the lower tail, at every q). Default integrator is now `method="gauss"`; `"hcubature"` retained for cross-checking. **The open decision, if the hold is reconsidered: making "gauss" the default changes returned values for every user — that is the one choice that becomes irreversible once on CRAN.** Gates all green: 424 tests pass (0 fail/warn/skip; 345 -> 424 after PR #30's coverage work), `R CMD check --as-cran` 0 errors/0 warnings (1 local-only NOTE, HTML-Tidy version, not CRAN-relevant), test coverage 71.70% (up from 55.45%), r-hub 3/3 pass (linux/windows/macos-arm64, 2026-08-17) **and re-run 3/3 `Status: OK` on the final tree `e557536` (2026-08-22 16:14 MDT, run 32601694146)**, win-builder 3/3 Status: OK — R-devel (r90413), R-release (4.6.1), R-oldrelease (4.5.3), all received 2026-08-17 and confirmed in Gmail 2026-08-21. `cran-comments.md` is