## Session 2026-10-11 (PR #36 merged: mbco() RAM-model fix + OpenMx oracle)
- **medfit route is BLOCKED, not started.** A `mbco()` method on a pair of medfit
  `SEMFit`s needs medfit's `anova()` for `SEMFit` and its nonlinear-constraint
  branch split (W3) merged in medfit dev first (medfit grill G10). Handoff:
  `medfit/planning/specs/HANDOFF-rmediation-mbco-on-mbco_sem-2026-10-11.md`
  (read-only from here). Nothing added to DESCRIPTION; the OpenMx path is
  unchanged apart from the class check below.
- **Unblocked part done:** known-answer fixture on `memory_exp`
  (`tests/testthat/helper-memory-exp-ram.R`, `test-mbco-memory-exp-oracle.R`):
  `mxCompare` diffLL 221.045546 (`a1 == 0`), 0.083100 (`b1 == 0`), minimum
  0.083100, df 1, tol 1e-6. Control: the `?mbco` example as written gives
  0.060332 (shifted labels). medfit compares its own result against these.
- **Bug found and fixed (PR #36, squash `771577a`):** `mbco()` rejected every
  fitted OpenMx RAM model ("h0 must be an MxModel") because the check compared
  `class(h0)` to `"MxModel"`; it now uses `methods::is()`. The `?mbco` example
  had shifted labels (`endVar` began with `"x"`) and passed a tibble to
  `mxData()`; both fixed, and it now tests `a*b = 0` as the smaller of two
  linear nulls. Verified for `type = "asymp"` only; `"parametric"` and `"semi"`
  have not been run on fitted RAM models. Suite: 452 expectations, 0 failed.
- **#35 stays open:** a single nonlinear null can converge to the wrong branch
  (`a1 = 0`, 221.05 vs the correct 0.0831). Documented in `?mbco` Details; the
  real fix is the medfit route above.
- **CI:** RMediation PR runs are 1-3 min and have no `skip_on_cran()` calls, so
  the NOT_CRAN tiering used in medrobust (#57 merged, #58 open) is not needed here.
- **Not applied:** `devtools::document()` with roxygen 8.1.0 reformats NAMESPACE
